ng.) We rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 17319, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DKMrskDXP18d6H4mVVqbPv", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17319, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DKMrskDXP18d6H4mVVqbPv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21590, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been marked unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now on it, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The title is \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0\". It explains the failure, the rollback and the current healthy state. It also says v2.3.1 shouldn't be deployed again until the cause is found. Before opening it I checked that no incident was already open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014JA7K98qgsZzVoRJDmEQcU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "con